# R10: each hero's Call to Adventure, a two-picture intro before the boarding (the Fate hook: every hero holds an unnoticed ticket).
# Plays once at a new game, one slide pair for each hero in the party, in this order; never shows a face. Started by the new-game hook (`calls_to_adventure:start`).
# The companions' reasons are tied to their wants and secrets in `Companions/` (HOOK(F): Lane F may sharpen a Call to its Thread's first line).
# The custom hero's Call is generic (`flag.party_has_custom`, set by the module at party creation). Drafted by Gemini (Gemini/sent_21_calls_to_adventure.txt), edited.

~ start
-> call_rook_coldwake_check

~ call_rook_coldwake_check
if name:rook_coldwake
cutscene gl_call_rook_coldwake
Narrator: Rook Coldwake presses a pale marker into the frozen battlefield mud to buy the restless dead a quiet night. Dry flower seeds spill from his iron gauntlet onto the frost.
cutscene gl_call_rook_coldwake_2
Narrator: The stone casts a long shadow across the ruts, and a black ticket with silver letters sits square on the cap. Even a warden gets summoned down the road.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Improper placement. No permit, no chiseled date, and the mortar isn't even set.
cutscene end
endif
-> call_tobin_hayward_check

~ call_tobin_hayward_check
if name:tobin_hayward
cutscene gl_call_tobin_hayward
Narrator: Tobin Hayward knots a wicker charm around a blighted wheat stalk with hands of stitched burlap and dry straw. He works the dead dirt like it still remembers spring.
cutscene gl_call_tobin_hayward_2
Narrator: One green shoot breaks the crust beside the rot, and a black ticket with silver letters rests in the wicker weave. The harvest comes in strange shapes out here.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good soil takes its time, I suppose, even when the weeds send invitations.
cutscene end
endif
-> call_silas_vane_check

~ call_silas_vane_check
if name:silas_vane
cutscene gl_call_silas_vane
Narrator: Silas Vane rifles a deck of carved bone slivers across a scarred alley table, chalk tallies stacked against his name. A man betting his own hide plays a tight hand.
cutscene gl_call_silas_vane_2
Narrator: He turns the river card and finds black pasteboard stamped in silver letters where the bones ought to be. The house always collects, one way or another.
interject name:silas_vane: Marked deck. Tell's in the silver ink, and the dealer didn't even leave a stack to steal.
cutscene end
endif
-> call_delphine_ravelle_check

~ call_delphine_ravelle_check
if name:delphine_ravelle
cutscene gl_call_delphine_ravelle
Narrator: On an empty midway past midnight, Delphine Ravelle pulls tight the thread in her patchwork cuff. Behind her on the canvas wall, a floating jester's shadow mouths a silent rhyme.
cutscene gl_call_delphine_ravelle_2
Narrator: Inside the torn lining of her notebook, silver letters gleam on a black ticket she never tucked away. Folks who sign with a grin always find another stage waiting.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: No applause, no advance billing, and the management leaves a pass in my seam. Simply shameless.
cutscene end
endif
-> call_lucan_houndstooth_check

~ call_lucan_houndstooth_check
if name:lucan_houndstooth
cutscene gl_call_lucan_houndstooth
Narrator: Lucan Houndstooth tracks heavy prints through the cold mire where a ghostly mastiff shows its ribs against the fog. That pale hound never points toward easy game.
cutscene gl_call_lucan_houndstooth_2
Narrator: The beast lifts its paw from the mud, leaving a black ticket with silver letters pinned clean to the earth. It is a mighty polite way for an omen to point.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Easy, boy. A strange scent on the wind, and the quarry seems to have sent its calling card.
cutscene end
endif
-> call_cordelia_skein_check

~ call_cordelia_skein_check
if name:cordelia_skein
cutscene gl_call_cordelia_skein
Narrator: Cordelia Skein spins crimson notes into the air above her glowing ruby vials, each silk letter dissolving before it cools. Stolen blood makes for a stubborn ink.
cutscene gl_call_cordelia_skein_2
Narrator: Deep in the corner cocoon, the threads have woven themselves around a black ticket stamped with silver letters. The answer to her riddle lives down the road.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Fascinating pathology. The silk rejects my notes, yet binds a foreign specimen without a single tremor.
cutscene end
endif
-> call_custom_check

~ call_custom_check
if flag.party_has_custom
cutscene gl_call_custom
Narrator: A traveler's hand rests on a cold door latch while the window lamp burns low inside. The nail where the house key hangs is bare as winter bone.
cutscene gl_call_custom_2
Narrator: Right where the iron key ought to sit, a black ticket catches the lamplight in sharp silver letters. When the road wants you, it locks the door behind you.
cutscene end
endif
-> finish

~ finish
quest ghostlight_express boarding
move ghostlight_boarding:default
